O6SJc7mzh4N","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T15:04:20Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T15:04:20Z","body":"Could the `api_type` entry be used to differentiate low-level APIs too (those not intended for scripting)? \r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12622","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3872267789/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3872757620","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114861#issuecomment-3872757620","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114861","id":3872757620,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7m1Zd0","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T16:25:04Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T16:25:04Z","body":"I don't think my PR is related to your proposal, except very loosely.\r\n\r\n* `api_type` is added here only for classes, not for functions (methods, constructors, operators).\r\n* As far as I understand, `api_type` doesn't indicate whether a class/function is accessible to high-level languages. It determines when the class is available (at what engine initialization level). For your proposal, a different attribute is needed.\r\n* We only need to make this attribute available in the XML documentation because this information is required for `make_rst.py` (class categorization). The built-in Editor Help could use the engine's internal API directly. If your purposes require filtering or somehow marking the low-level API in online documentation, then yes, with the current approach, we need to add the attribute to the XML documentation.\r\n  * In theory, we could avoid this by providing a separate command-line option that `make_rst.py` could use to query the necessary information. However, `make_rst.py` currently generates online Class References solely from XML documentation, which is synchronized using `--doctool`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"http